description:
FILED s515a (Opus, 2026-10-11) from #3185's edge probes.  PRE-EXISTING (same output on s514f's tip 8c683ae6).

`local *STDOUT` does not localize the glob's IO slot (tie-aggregates.md section 7: only a tie PLACEHOLDER made inside the scope is undone), so a tie of an OPENED handle inside `local *STDOUT` keys on the real STDOUT stream and SURVIVES the scope: every later print goes to the tie object.

    package Obj; sub TIEHANDLE { bless {}, shift } sub PRINT { 1 }
    package main;
    { local *STDOUT; tie *STDOUT, 'Obj'; print "hidden\n"; }
    print "end\n";

perl 5.40.3: `end`.   PCL: nothing (silent wrong; rc 0).

Fix direction: %p-glob-restore-tied-io (the local *FH undo) should also drop a tie record made inside the scope on a stream that was the glob's IO at the save (record the tie's owner glob + a scope serial), or `local *FH` should localize the IO slot for real (perl does: inside the scope *STDOUT has no IO at all, so the tie gets a placeholder).  Probe the Capture::Tiny `local *STDOUT` shapes before choosing.
